# ---- correspondence and editorial drafts: kept locally, not part of the record ----
# PeerJ reviews single-blind and the review letters are not part of the published article.
source/admin/

# ---- third-party material that is not ours to redistribute ----
# peerj-20977.pdf is a PUBLISHED PeerJ paper by other authors, downloaded only to compare
# our typesetting against a real example. It is not ours and must never be pushed.
peerj-20977.pdf
symmetry_corpus/
nuo_fulltext/
MDPI_template_APA.zip

# The PDF PeerJ's own production pipeline generated from our submission, returned to the
# authors as peerj-reviewing-150843-v0.pdf. It is PeerJ's file, it carries the editorial
# furniture ("Manuscript to be reviewed", "Important declarations"), and it is the artefact
# the glyph-corruption analysis was measured against -- so it is worth keeping locally, and
# it must not be published as part of the submission.
peerj-reviewing-*.pdf
Author-Cover-Page-Template.doc

# ---- withdrawn venues: kept on disk, deliberately NOT part of this repository ----
# These tarballs hold the MDPI/Symmetry and Taylor & Francis/IJGIS builds that were
# withdrawn. They are kept locally so the work is not lost, but this repository is the
# PeerJ submission and must contain PeerJ material only, so they are excluded from it.
source/archive/

# ---- NOT ignored: uo_sensor_cache.json - it is REQUIRED ----
# This file was briefly excluded on a wrong assumption. It is an INPUT, not a cache that can
# be rebuilt: `longitudinal_census.py` and `census_model.py` both read it, and CI runs both.
# Without it the census cannot be regenerated from the checkout, so there is deliberately NO
# ignore rule for it -- see the note in the repository README.
#
# It is safe to publish, and the manuscript says so itself. Its Data Availability statement
# describes this exact artefact: "the one-week instrument catalogue the snapshot audit is
# computed from ... a list of instruments -- identity, position, broker and variable names
# -- and every measured quantity in it has been removed; no temperature, concentration or
# count is redistributed". Checked directly: the file holds 1906 instruments with lon/lat,
# name, theme and variable, plus the archive FILENAMES each appears in. No reading, no value,
# no concentration. It is the same kind of catalogue already published in the Zenodo deposit.

